# Lessons

Cross-cycle anti-patterns and rules. Each lesson is one H2 with a memorable name, a one-paragraph rule, and a `Why:` line citing the cycle(s) that produced it.

The curator surfaces a lesson candidate when:

- An anti-pattern is caught by `@code-reviewer` or `@security-auditor` in 2+ cycles.
- A `REFACTOR` gate decision generalises beyond the cycle that produced it.
- The owner explicitly says "remember this for next time" during a HITL gate.

The curator de-duplicates lessons (same idea under two H2s) during Mode B.

