## Name 3, build once

A reusable abstraction earns its place only when **three known consumers** exist in the codebase. Two consumers is a watchlist entry. One consumer is just a function — keep it inline.

**Why:** Premature abstraction costs more than three local copies. The third consumer is the signal that the contract has stabilised.

**How to apply:** When proposing a `wiki/patterns/` page, list all three consumer file paths. If only two are present, file a watchlist comment in the curator's diff and revisit when a third lands.

